ps - show process status

SYNOPSIS
    ps [pid ...]

DESCRIPTION
    Print a snapshot to standard output. With no operands, show all
    active processes. Supply process IDs to select particular rows.

    The columns are process ID, parent ID, process group, user ID,
    group ID, state, address space size in bytes, and command name.
    R is runnable or running, S is sleeping, T is stopped, and Z is
    a zombie waiting to be collected.

EXAMPLES
    ps | grep sh
    ps 1 2

SEE ALSO
    kill(1), sh(1), waitpid(2)
